\n48: Total fee paid:\n49: ý\n50: Fee paid previously with preliminary materials.\n51: o\n52: Check box if any part of the fee is offset as provided by Exchange Act Rule 0-11(a)(2) and identify the filing for which the offsetting fee was paid previously. Identify the previous filing by registration\n53: statement number, or the Form or Schedule and the date of its filing.\n54: (1)\n55: Amount Previously Paid:\n56: (2)\n57: Form, Schedule or Registration Statement No.:\n58: (3)\n59: Filing Party:\n60: (4)\n61: Date Filed:\n62: Table of Contents\n63: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n64: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n65: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n66: December 4, 2013\n67: Dear\n68: Stockholder:\n69: You\n70: are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\") to be held on Wednesday, January 8, 2014, at\n71: 10:00 a.m. local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n72: LLP\n73: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street, Boston, Massachusetts 02109\n74: (the \"special meeting\").\n75: At\n76: the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to adopt a merger agreement pursuant to which Mac-Gray would be acquired by Spin Holdco Inc. a\n77: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., and other related proposals. We entered into the merger agreement on October 14, 2013. If the merger is completed, you will be entitled\n78: to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less any applicable withholding taxes, for each share of Mac-Gray common stock that you own.\n79: The\n80: Mac-Gray Board of Directors formed a special committee of six disinterested and independent directors to, among other things, review and evaluate the merger agreement proposal,\n81: consider and evaluate alternatives available to Mac-Gray and alleviate any potential conflicts of interest. After careful consideration, our Board of Directors, upon the unanimous recommendation of\n82: the special committee, unanimously approved the merger agreement and determined that the merger and the other transactions contemplated by the merger agreement are advisable and in the best interests\n83: of Mac-Gray and our stockholders. Our Board of Directors unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" the adoption of the merger agreement.\n84: At\n85: the special meeting, in addition to the approval of the merger agreement, you will be asked to cast an advisory (non-binding) vote on the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or\n86: that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing arrangements. Our Board of Directors\n87: unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" approval, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, of the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of\n88: Mac-Gray in connection with the merger.\n89: Your vote is important, regardless of the number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock you own.\n90: We cannot consummate the merger unless the\n91: merger\n92: agreement is adopted by the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding shares of Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting. If you abstain from voting, fail to cast your\n93: vote, in person or by proxy, or fail to give voting instructions to your brokerage firm, bank, trust or other nominee, it will have the same effect as a vote against the proposal to adopt the merger\n94: agreement.\n95: The\n96: attached proxy statement provides you with detailed information about the special meeting, the merger agreement and the merger. A copy of the merger agreement is attached as\n97: Annex A to the proxy statement. We encourage you to read the proxy statement and the merger agreement carefully and in their entirety. You may also obtain more information about Mac-Gray from\n98: documents we have filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission.\n99: On\n100: behalf of your Board of Directors, thank you for your continued support and interest in Mac-Gray Corporation. I look forward to seeing you at the meeting on January 8, 2014.\n101: Very\n102: truly yours,\n103: STEWART GRAY MACDONALD, JR.\n104: Chief Executive Officer\n105: Table of Contents\n106: Your vote is very important regardless of the number of shares you own. At your earliest convenience, please vote by telephone or via the Internet according to\n107: the instructions provided on the enclosed proxy card or complete, sign, date and return the enclosed proxy card, which requires no postage if mailed in the United States.\n108: Stockholders with questions or requiring assistance voting their shares may contact MacKenzie Partners, Inc., our proxy solicitor:\n109: 105\n110: Madison Avenue\n111: New York, NY 10016\n112: proxy@mackenziepartners.com\n113: (212) 929-5500 (Call Collect)\n114: or\n115: TOLL FREE 1-800-322-2885\n116: Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities regulatory agency has approved or disapproved the merger, passed upon the merits or\n117: fairness of the merger or passed upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\n118: This\n119: proxy statement is dated December 4, 2013 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about December 4, 2013.\n120: Table of Contents\n121: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n122: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n123: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n124: (781) 487-7600\n125: NOTICE OF THE SPECIAL MEETING OF STOCKHOLDERS\n126: TO BE HELD ON JANUARY 8, 2014\n127: NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation, a Delaware corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\"), will be held on\n128: Wednesday, January 8, 2014 at 10:00 a.m., local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n129: LLP\n130: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street,\n131: Boston, Massachusetts 02109 (together with adjournments or postponements thereof, the \"special meeting\") for the following purposes:\n132: 1.     To\n133: consider and vote on a proposal to adopt the Agreement and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 14, 2013, by and among CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc., a\n134: Delaware corporation (\"Holdings\"), CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., a Delaware corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of Holdings (\"CSC\"), Spin Holdco Inc., a Delaware corporation and\n135: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC (\"Parent\" and, together with Holdings and CSC, the \"Buyer Entities\") and CSC Fenway, Inc., a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent (\"Merger\n136: Subsidiary\") and Mac-Gray, as it may be amended from time to time, pursuant to which Mac-Gray will be merged with Merger Subsidiary with Mac-Gray surviving the merger as a wholly-owned subsidiary of\n137: Parent;\n138: 2.     To\n139: consider and vote on an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive\n140: officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements;\n141: 3.     To\n142: consider and vote on a proposal to approve one or more adjournments or postponements of the special meeting, if necessary, to solicit additional proxies if Mac-Gray\n143: has not obtained sufficient affirmative stockholder votes to adopt the merger agreement; and\n144: 4.     To\n145: transact such other business as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of the special meeting.\n146: The\n147: Board of Directors has fixed the close of business on November 27, 2013 as the record date for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n148: and any adjournments or postponements thereof. Only holders of Mac-Gray's common stock of record at the close of business on that date will be entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n149: and any adjournments or postponements thereof.\n150: Under\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 151]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/macgray_text.txt, lines 1-150\n1: DEFM14A\n2: 1\n3: a2217482zdefm14a.htm\n4: DEFM14A\n5: Use these links to rapidly review the document\n6: Table of Contents\n7: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n8: Table of Contents\n9: UNITED STATES\n10: SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION\n11: Washington, D.C. 20549\n12: SCHEDULE 14A\n13: Proxy\n14: Statement Pursuant to Section 14(a) of\n15: the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (Amendment No.          )\n16: Filed by the Registrant\n17: ý\n18: Filed by a Party other than the Registrant\n19: o\n20: Check the appropriate box:\n21: o\n22: Preliminary Proxy Statement\n23: o\n24: Confidential, for Use of the Commission Only (as permitted by Rule 14a-6(e)(2))\n25: ý\n26: Definitive Proxy Statement\n27: o\n28: Definitive Additional Materials\n29: o\n30: Soliciting Material under §240.14a-12\n31: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n32: (Name of Registrant as Specified In Its Charter)\n33: (Name of Person(s) Filing Proxy Statement, if other than the Registrant)\n34: Payment of Filing Fee (Check the appropriate box):\n35: o\n36: No fee required.\n37: o\n38: Fee computed on table below per Exchange Act Rules 14a-6(i)(1) and 0-11.\n39: (1)\n40: Title of each class of securities to which transaction applies:\n41: (2)\n42: Aggregate number of securities to which transaction applies:\n43: (3)\n44: Per unit price or other underlying value of transaction computed pursuant to Exchange Act Rule 0-11 (set forth the amount on which the filing fee is calculated and state how it was determined):\n45: (4)\n46: Proposed maximum aggregate value of transaction:\n47: (5)\n48: Total fee paid:\n49: ý\n50: Fee paid previously with preliminary materials.\n51: