: CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.,\n356: with over one million machines in service, is the leading provider of multi-family housing and commercial\n357: laundry solutions as well as the industry leader in air vending services at convenience stores and gas stations. CSC's family of businesses includes: Coinmach Corp., ASI Campus Laundry Solutions, SDI\n358: Laundry Solutions, Sparkle Solutions Corp., Appliance Warehouse of America, AIR-serv, AirValet and Super Laundry. CSC has a workforce of over 2,250 dedicated professionals throughout the United\n359: States, Canada and Europe.\n360: CSC\n361: ServiceWorks, Inc.\n362: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n363: Plainview, New York 11803\n364: (516) 349-8555\n365: CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n366: is a Delaware corporation and the sole stockholder of CSC.\n367: CSC\n368: ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n369: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n370: Plainview, New York 11803\n371: (516) 349-8555\n372: 2\n373: Table of Contents\n374: Spin Holdco Inc.\n375: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC.\n376: Spin\n377: Holdco Inc.\n378: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n379: Plainview, New York 11803\n380: (516) 349-8555\n381: CSC Fenway, Inc.\n382: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent.\n383: CSC\n384: Fenway, Inc.\n385: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n386: Plainview, New York 11803\n387: (516) 349-8555\n388: The Special Meeting (Page 20)\n389: Date, Time and Place.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 390]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/macgray_text.txt, lines 320-389\n320: •\n321: the impact of the pending merger on Mac-Gray's strategic plans and operations and Mac-Gray's ability to respond\n322: effectively to competitive pressures, industry developments and future opportunities; and\n323: •\n324: other risks detailed in Mac-Gray's filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission, or SEC, including Mac-G