one call, without identifying Party A, Party B, Party C or CSC/Pamplona and without indicating any proposed\n1662:[p35] alternatives process, and the negotiations between Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona so that Mr. MacDonald could consider whether he continued to have an interest in potentially rolling over any of his\n1665:[p35] on September 11, 2013, the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona.\n1669:[p35] indications of interest. BofA Merrill Lynch then indicated that, based on conversations with Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona, it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in\n1676:[p36] without knowing that Mr. MacDonald would support the transaction. Based on the amount of due diligence conducted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona, and discussions with such parties\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && grep -n \\\"Pamplona\\\" macgray_paged.txt | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825316461,"end":1789825316596}}}}
