{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825407105,"sessionID":"ses_f461ef367ffe0p6nB1IHi4bUUU","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e844b5001ldGT9oUaM9IIiz","sessionID":"ses_f461ef367ffe0p6nB1IHi4bUUU","messageID":"msg_0b9e8335e001ZeV0u3Esb2Odc7","type":"tool","id":"call_00_GubFRzkCCQf811PEfBjv7579","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, bisect\n\nraw = open('macgray_text.txt').read()\nlines = raw.replace('\\xa0',' ').split('\\n')\n\nfooters=[]; expected=1\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines):\n    if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{1,3}', l.strip()) and i>300:\n        n=int(l)\n        if n==expected:\n            footers.append((i+1,n)); expected+=1\nfooter_lines=[f[0] for f in footers]; footer_pages=[f[1] for f in footers]\ndef page_of(line):\n    idx=bisect.bisect_left(footer_lines,line)\n    return footer_pages[idx] if idx<len(footer_pages) else None\n\n# collapsed text with page map\nchars=[]; pagemap=[]\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines):\n    t=' '.join(l.split())\n    if t=='' : continue\n    if chars: \n        chars.append(' '); pagemap.append(page_of(i+1))\n    for ch in t:\n        chars.append(ch); pagemap.append(page_of(i+1))\nflat=''.join(chars)\nprint(\"flat len\", len(flat))\n\ndef find(q):\n    parts=[p.strip() for p in q.split('...')]\n    idx=flat.find(parts[0])\n    while idx!=-1:\n        pos=idx; ok=True; spans=[]\n        spans.append((idx, idx+len(parts[0])))\n        for p in parts[1:]:\n            nxt=flat.find(p,pos)\n            if nxt==-1: ok=False; break\n            spans.append((nxt,nxt+len(p)))\n            pos=nxt+len(p)\n        if ok:\n            pages=set()\n            for a,b in spans:\n                for j in range(a,b): pages.add(pagemap[j])\n            return idx, pos, sorted(pages), spans\n        idx=flat.find(parts[0], idx+1)\n    return None\n\nquotes = {\n 'q2': \"authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities that might be available to Mac-Gray, including opportunities with another strategic party\",\n 'q3': \"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray\",\n 'q4': \"On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions\",\n 'q6': \"Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees\",\n 'q7': \"Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share\",\n 'q9': \"they had spoken with representatives of Pamplona, as instructed by the Special Committee, who expressed interest in a transaction, including an acquisition of Mac-Gray by its portfolio company, CSC\",\n 'q10': \"15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers\",\n 'q11': \"BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting\",\n 'q12': \"Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n 'q13': \"On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n 'q14': \"decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that the potential equity rollover of Moab's shares could be available as a source of capital\",\n 'q15': \"On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package\",\n 'q18': \"On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\",\n 'q19': \"On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share\",\n 'q20': \"representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share\",\n 'q21': \"authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure ... and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings\",\n 'q22': \"Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share\",\n 'q23': \"On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n 'q24': \"Party B and Party C ... were given broad access to an electronic data site, and Party A and CSC/Pamplona ... were given somewhat limited access\",\n 'q25': \"sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\",\n 'q27': \"CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required\",\n 'q28': \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\",\n 'q29': \"Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources\",\n 'q30': \"a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share\",\n 'q32': \"request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\",\n 'q33': \"CSC/Pam