red\" (p. 36) | sort=2013-09-18 00:00:00 from=2013-09-18 00:00:00 to=2013-09-18 00:00:00\n#37 | 09/18/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid reaffirmed | P1 R3 | 18-19 | Yes | Formal | Heavy | n=1 | None | inf=None | None\n    note: Confirmed its standing offer as best and final, declining to improve; financing not committed so Heavy; out when exclusivity executed (see #43).\n    quote: \"its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\" (p. 36) | sort=2013-09-18 00:00:00 from=2013-09-18 00:00:00 to=2013-09-18 00:00:00\n#38 | 09/18/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | P1 R3 | 21.5-21.5 | No | Formal | Heavy | n=1 | None | inf=None | None\n    note: revises #30; $19.00 cash at closing plus options (10% of new equity, strike at cost basis) valued by Party B at $2.50/share; financing not committed.\n    quote: \"submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing\" (p. 36) | sort=2013-09-18 00:00:00 from=2013-09-18 00:00:00 to=2013-09-18 00:00:00\n#39 | 09/18/2013 | Party C | Financial | Did not submit | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n=1 | Not stated | inf=None | {Q4}\n    note: No revised indication at the final request and no reasons given; not mentioned again.\n    quote: \"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest ... nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith\" (p. 36) | sort=2013-09-18 00:00:00 from=2013-09-18 00:00:00 to=2013-09-18 00:00:00\n#40 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Other material event | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | {Q1}\n    note: Selected CSC/Pamplona as preferred bidder and set $21.25 per share for exclusivity; Party B's option-heavy bid considered less certain; MacDonald supportive.\n    quote: \"authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\" (p. 37) | sort=2013-09-19 00:00:00 from=2013-09-19 00:00:00 to=2013-09-19 00:00:00\n#41 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | P1 R3 | 21.25-21.25 | Yes | Formal | Light | n=1 | None | inf=None | {Q1}\n    note: revises #36; last and best offer tied to two-week exclusive negotiations; no financing contingency; MacDonald voting agreements requested.\n    quote: \"CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer\" (p. 37) | sort=2013-09-21 00:00:00 from=2013-09-21 00:00:00 to=2013-09-21 00:00:00\n#42 | 09/24/2013 | CSC/Pamplona |  | Exclusivity changed | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | {Q6}\n    note: Executed (authorized 09/23): exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to no adverse change to the final proposal.\n    quote: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\" (p. 38) | sort=2013-09-24 00:00:00 from=2013-09-24 00:00:00 to=2013-09-24 00:00:00\n#43 | by 09/24/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Dropped by target | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n=1 | Would not improve earlier offer | inf=Y | {Q5}\n    note: Inferred: out when the target executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona; its 09/18 best-and-final declined to improve.\n    quote: \"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations\" (p. 38) | sort=2013-09-24 00:00:00 from=None to=2013-09-24 00:00:00\n#44 | by 09/24/2013 | Party B | Financial | Dropped by target | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n=1 | Not stated | inf=Y | {Q5}\n    note: Inferred: out when exclusivity executed; the target had preferred CSC/Pamplona's certainty after weighing Party B's option-heavy $21.50 bid.\n    quote: \"CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations\" (p. 38) | sort=2013-09-24 00:00:00 from=None to=2013-09-24 00:00:00\n#45 | 09/25/2013 | Kirkland & Ellis LLP |  | Adviser | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | None\n    note: Outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; first seen acting 09/25/2013 when the initial merger agreement draft was delivered to it.\n    quote: \"Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\" (p. 38) | sort=2013-09-25 00:00:00 from=2013-09-25 00:00:00 to=2013-09-25 00:00:00\n#46 | by 10/07/2013 | Moab |  | Other material event | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | None\n    note: Rollover resolved: after Pamplona discussions (facilitated 09/23, continuing to 10/07), Moab determined not to roll over; Rothenberg then briefed.\n    quote: \"after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction\" (p. 39) | sort=2013-10-07 00:00:00 from=None to=2013-10-07 00:00:00\n#47 | 10/12/2013 | CSC/Pamplona |  | Exclusivity changed | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | {Q1}\n    note: Extended to 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013 (requested by CSC/Pamplona and authorized 10/09) as negotiations continued.\n    quote: \"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013\" (p. 41) | sort=2013-10-12 00:00:00 from=2013-10-12 00:00:00 to=2013-10-12 00:00:00\n#48 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona |  | Merger agreement signed | P1 R3 | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | None\n    note: Board approved on the Special Committee's recommendation; $21.25/share cash; no financing contingency; Pamplona commitment letter delivered; $11M Mac-Gray and $15M reverse termination fees.\n    quote: \"on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered\" (p. 41) | sort=2013-10-14 00:00:00 from=2013-10-14 00:00:00 to=2013-10-14 00:00:00\n#49 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC |  | Merger announced | P Rpost | - | None | None | None | n= | None | inf=None | None\n    note: Joint announcement before the U.S. markets opened; $21.25 per share in cash.\n    quote: \"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement\" (p. 41) | sort=2013-10-15 00:00:00 from=2013-10-15 00:00:00 to=2013-10-15 00:00:00\n\n=== Rounds ===\nProcess || Round || Opened || How opened || Who was in || Due dates || Deadline outcome || Finality || Bids received || How it ended\n1 || 0 || None || Pre-process: Party A interest 04/08; unsolicited proposal 06/21 || None admitted; Party A live with a standing offer || none stated || No deadline stated || Not final || 1: Party A $17.00-$19.00 || Party A's standing offer carried into round 1\n1 || 1 || 2013-06-24 00:00:00 || Special Committee concluded a sale should be considered; determined to approach 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial); outreach began within days || 20 NDA signers: 2 strategic (Party A 08/05, CSC/Pamplona 07/11); 18 financial incl. Party B 06/28, Party C 06/30 || 07/23/2013 || Late bids accepted || Not final || 3: CSC/Pamplona $18.50; Party B $17.00-$18.00; Party C $15.00-$17.00 oral, then $16.00-$16.50 written || four advanced; sixteen residual signers out\n1 || 2 || 2013-07-25 00:00:00 || Four IOI bidders advanced to staged disclosure and management meetings; revised IOIs requested || 4: Party A (Strategic), CSC/Pamplona (Strategic), Party B (Financial), Party C (Financial) || 09/09/2013 || Late bids accepted || Not final || 4: CSC/Pamplona $19.50; Party B $18.50; Party A $18.00-$19.00; Party C $16.00-$17.00 || three advanced; Party C out\n1 || 3 || 2013-09-11 00:00:00 || Final indications of interest requested by 09/18; short exclusive negotiations possible || 4: Party A (Strategic), CSC/Pamplona (Strategic), Party B (Financial), Party C (Financial) || 09/18/2013 || Enforced || Announced as final || 3: CSC/Pamplona $20.75 then $21.25; Party B $21.50 (valued); Party A $18.00-$19.00 reaffirmed || CSC/Pamplona advanced to exclusivity; signing\n\n=== Questions ===\nQ || Question || Recommended answer || Why, with page || Rows affected || What changes if answered differently || Reviewer note\nQ1 || Round map: one process; round 1 opened 06/24/2013 by the Special Committee's decision to approach 50 parties; round 2 on 07/25/2013 (four advanced to staged diligence and revised IOIs); round 3 on 09/11/2013 (final indications due 09/18); the 09/19-09/24 price increase and exclusivity sit inside round 3. Correct? || Keep the map: rounds 1-3 as dated; round 0 holds the pre-process events (04/08 Party A contact; 06/21 proposal); the exclusive stage is not a fourth round. || C8: a round opens when the target selects who advances and seeks updated offers (pp. 31, 34), and final/best-and-final requests open one even with unchanged bidders (p. 36); 'exclusivity inside an established final stage' is not a new round. || #9-#11, #23, #34, #40-#42, #43-#44, #47 || Starting round 1 at the 06/28 first reported outreach moves #9-#11; treating the exclusive stage as round 4 adds a Round opened row and reassigns the 09/19-10/14 rows (#40 to #48). || None\nQ2 || Round 1's 07/23/2013 due date: CSC/Pamplona submitted on time; Party B (07/24) and Party C (07/24 oral; 07/25 written) arrived after it but were reviewed on 07/25. 'Late bids accepted'? || Late bids accepted - they were considered with no recorded extension. || C11: a bid is late only if its Date from is after the due date; both late arrivals were reviewed at the 07/25 meeting (p. 34), and no Deadline revised row exists. || #17-#21, #24 || Enforced would drop the late-bid reading for Party B and Party C; an Extended reading would add a Deadline revised row. || None\nQ3 || Round 2's 09/09/2013 due date: CSC/Pamplona and Party B on time; Party A and Party C submitted 09/10 and were reviewed 09/11. 'Late bids accepted'? || Late bids accepted - they were considered with no recorded extension. || C11; both Dates from fall after the 08/27 letter's 09/09 deadline (p. 35); the Special Committee reviewed them on 09/11 (p. 36). || #28-#32 || Enforced would remove the late reading; a de facto extension reading would add a Deadline revised row and change the round-2 outcome. || None\nQ4 || Round 3's 09/18/2013 due date: three bids arrived; Party C neither submitted nor reiterated. 'Enforced', with Party C exiting as Did not submit at the due date? || Enforced; Party C Did not submit on 09/18 (not necessarily permanent, but never mentioned again). || C11 Enforced = the target's next step on the bids in hand (09/19 preferred-bidder decision, p. 37); C16 Did not submit; Party C's absence is reported at p. 36. || #35, #39 || If Party C were still live at exclusivity, add a Dropped by target exit at 09/24 and count 4->3 only from #42. || None\nQ5 || Exit reasons for the two rivals displaced at exclusivity (inferred exits, 09/24): Party A 'Would not improve earlier offer' and Party B 'Not stated'? || Party A: Would not improve earlier offer (its 09/18 call was best and final). Party B: Not stated (no bidder-stated reason; the target-side certainty preference is reported, not Party B's reason). || C16: 'A bidder that is asked to improve and declines takes Would not improve earlier offer'; Party A declined (p. 36). Inferred exits default to Not stated (C16). || #43, #44 || Both Not stated would drop Party A's reported refusal to improve; 'Terms or process' for Party B would attribute the target's certainty preference to Party B. || None\nQ6 || Winner type: CSC/Pamplona as Strategic (sponsor-owned operating company, Pamplona providing financing support), or Mixed as a joint bid by an operator and a fund? || Strategic. CSC is an operating laundry company owned by Pamplona; Pamplona's role is committed financing support, and the filing counts CSC/Pamplona among the strategic bidders. || C3 ('including a sponsor-owned operating company'; 'not a strategic buyer with financing support'); the filing's own count at p. 32; Pamplona commitment at pp. 38, 59. || #12, #16, #19, #29, #36, #41, #42, #48 || Mixed would reinterpret the winner's type across its rows; no prices or counts change. || None\nQ7 || Initiation: 'Target-led' or 'Mixed'? The Board authorized exploration first (04/05) and its banker approached Party A (04/08), but Party A then bid unsolicited (06/21) and Moab was an activist presence. || Target-led - the Board's authorization and banker approach came first; the unsolicited proposal and Moab's activism shaped, but did not start, the process. || C6; pp. 27 (04/05 authorization; 04/08 contact), 29 (Moab proxy contest), 30 (Party A proposal). || #2, #3, #8 || Mixed would change the Deal facts initiation classification and flag bidder and activist influence. || None\n\n=== Deal facts ===\nField || Value\nTarget || Mac-Gray Corporation (Waltham, Massachusetts; laundry facilities management)\nAcquirer || CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. and affiliates (Spin Holdco Inc., CSC Fenway Inc.), funded by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P.\nAcquirer type || Strategic - sponsor-owned operating company (Pamplona-owned CSC; laundry services)\nAgreed price and consideration || $21.25 per share in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes\nMerger agreement signed || 2013-10-14 00:00:00\nMerger announced || 2013-10-15 00:00:00\nFiling type and date || DEFM14A definitive proxy statement, dated December 4, 2013\nBackground pages || pp. 27-41\nInitiation || Target-led (Board authorized exploration 04/05/2013; banker approached Party A 04/08; unsolicited Party A proposal 06/21; Moab activist involvement)\nNumber of processes || 1\nAuction screen || Met - 20 confidentiality agreements with prospective acquirers (2 strategic, 18 financial)\nWhole-company bids || Yes - all four bidders bid for the whole company\nCurrency and units of bid prices || US dollars; per share\nTarget financial advisers || BofA Merrill Lynch (sole; engaged 05/31/2013; prior 2011-2012 mandate ended 05/15/2013)\nTarget legal advisers || Goodwin Procter LLP\nAccount || Mac-Gray, a laundry facilities management company, ran one sale process. After the Board authorized exploration in April 2013 and its banker approached Party A, an unsolicited Party A proposal in June ($17.00-$19.00) led the Special Committee to solicit 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial) on June 24; 20 signed confidentiality agreements and four bid seriously: CSC/Pamplona and Party A (both strategic), and financial bidders Party B and Party C. Round 1 indications (due July 23) were judged low; the four advanced to management meetings and revised indications (due September 9), then to final indications (due September 18). CSC/Pamplona led at every stage ($18.50, $19.50, $20.75), Party B put the highest headline value on September 18 ($21.50 per share as valued, cash plus options), and Party C dropped out at the final deadline. On September 19 the Special Committee chose CSC/Pamplona, secured $21.25 per share with exclusivity on September 24, and signed the merger agreement on October 14, 2013, announced October 15.\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re, bisect, datetime as dt\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\\nprint(\\\"=== DEAL LEDGER ===\\\")\\nhdr=[c.value for c in ws[1]]\\nfor r in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\\n    vals=[ws.cell(r,c).value for c in range(1, ws.max_column+1)]\\n    if r==1:\\n        print(\\\" | \\\".join(str(v) for v in vals)); print(\\\"-\\\"*100); continue\\n    line = f\\\"#{vals[0]} | {vals[1]} | {vals[2]} | {vals[3] or ''} | {vals[4]} | P{vals[5] if vals[5] is not None else ''} R{vals[6]} | {vals[7] if vals[7] is not None else ''}-{vals[8] if vals[8] is not None else ''} | {vals[9]} | {vals[10]} | {vals[11]} | n={vals[12] if vals[12] is not None else ''} | {vals[13]} | inf={vals[14]} | {vals[17]}\\\"\\n    print(line)\\n    print(f\\\"    note: {vals[15]}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"    quote: {vals[16]} | sort={vals[19]} from={vals[20]} to={vals[21]}\\\")\\nprint()\\nfor name in ('Rounds','Questions','Deal facts'):\\n    s=wb[name]\\n    print(f\\\"=== {name} ===\\\")\\n    for r in range(1,s.max_row+1):\\n        vals=[s.cell(r,c).value for c in range(1,s.max_column+1)]\\n        print(\\\" || \\\".join(str(v) for v in vals))\\n    print()\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825634766,"end":1789825636224}}}}
