{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825672695,"sessionID":"ses_f461ef367ffe0p6nB1IHi4bUUU","part":{"id":"prt_0b9ec2a660010WdIsko6duQI7J_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f461ef367ffe0p6nB1IHi4bUUU","messageID":"msg_0b9ec2a660010WdIsko6duQI7J","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and passes all verification checks. Here's the final deliverable.\n\n**Saved:** `extraction/mac-gray.xlsx` — four sheets in order (Deal ledger, Rounds, Questions, Deal facts), 49 ledger rows, header row 1 frozen, filters and wrap on, real dates formatted MM/DD/YYYY, no merged cells. Every quote was re-verified character-for-character against the filing with its printed page.\n\n## The sale, in short\n\nMac-Gray (laundry facilities management) ran **one** target-led process in 2013. After the board authorized exploration (04/05) and BofA Merrill Lynch approached **Party A** (04/08), Party A's unsolicited all-cash bid of $17.00–$19.00 (06/21) prompted the Special Committee to solicit **50 parties** (15 strategic, 35 financial) on 06/24. **20 signed confidentiality agreements** (2 strategic, 18 financial) and four bid seriously: **CSC/Pamplona** and **Party A** (strategic), **Party B** and **Party C** (financial).\n\n- **Round 1** (opened 06/24, IOIs due 07/23): CSC/Pamplona $18.50; Party B $17.00–$18.00; Party C $15.00–$17.00 then $16.00–$16.50. The four advanced.\n- **Round 2** (opened 07/25, revised IOIs due 09/09): CSC/Pamplona $19.50; Party B $18.50; Party A $18.00–$19.00; Party C $16.00–$17.00. Only financial bidders got broad data-site access; customer data withheld because both bidders' conditions were heavy (no committed financing, pre/limited diligence). Moab's rollover ambition was denied (07/06) and Mr. MacDonald declined to roll over (09/11).\n- **Round 3** (opened 09/11, final IOIs due 09/18): CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party B $21.50 *as valued* ($19.00 cash + options); Party A reaffirmed $18.00–$19.00 as best and final; **Party C dropped out**.\n- On 09/19 Mac-Gray selected CSC/Pamplona and required $21.25 for exclusivity; **$21.25 last-and-best** was agreed 09/21, exclusivity executed 09/24 (extended to 10/15), Party A and Party B inferred dropped; agreement signed **10/14/2013**, announced **10/15/2013**.\n\n## Open questions (full text on the Questions sheet, with recommendations)\n\n1. **Round/process map** (Q1) — keep rounds 1–3 as dated (06/24, 07/25, 09/11), round 0 for pre-process events, exclusivity inside round 3; alternative would open round 1 on the 06/28 outreach or add a fourth round for the exclusive stage.\n2. **Round-1 deadline** (Q2) — \"Late bids accepted\" (Party B/C arrived 07/24–25 and were reviewed).\n3. **Round-2 deadline** (Q3) — \"Late bids accepted\" (Party A/C arrived 09/10).\n4. **Round-3 deadline / Party C** (Q4) — \"Enforced\"; Party C exited as Did not submit on 09/18.\n5. **Rival exit reasons** (Q5) — Party A \"Would not improve earlier offer\"; Party B \"Not stated\".\n6. **Winner type** (Q6) — CSC/Pamplona is Strategic (sponsor-owned operating company; Pamplona is financing support, not a Mixed joint bid).\n7. **Initiation** (Q7) — Target-led, not Mixed.\n\n## What I could not do\n\nExact contact dates inside the June–July outreach wave, the signing dates and individual identities of the 16 unnamed NDA signers, and the precise day Moab's no-rollover decision was reached are not reported; those cells use the filing's windows and are marked as cohort/inferred rows (flagged in Q1/Q4/Q5 where the call could go the other way).","time":{"start":1789825657456,"end":1789825672695}}}
